WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.210
- We were just talking about
how music impacts everyone,

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:04.310
hearing and deaf.

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:06.630
And in the film 'Amelia's'
character auditions

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:08.980
to get into Berkeley College of Music,

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:12.570
one of, if not the best
music school in the country.

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:13.690
Let's see this audition.

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:15.307
(screen whooshing)
(classical music)

00:00:15.307 --> 00:00:20.307
♪ I've looked at love that way ♪

00:00:21.097 --> 00:00:25.866
♪ But now it's just another show ♪

00:00:25.866 --> 00:00:30.866
♪ You leave 'em laughing when you go ♪

00:00:31.495 --> 00:00:36.495
♪ And if you care, don't let 'em know ♪

00:00:37.791 --> 00:00:42.791
♪ Don't give yourself away ♪

00:00:43.552 --> 00:00:48.284
♪ I've looked at love
from both sides now ♪

00:00:48.284 --> 00:00:51.398
♪ From give and take ♪

00:00:51.398 --> 00:00:54.020
♪ And still somehow ♪

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:59.020
♪ It's love's illusions I recall ♪

00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:04.630
♪ I really don't know love ♪

00:01:09.188 --> 00:01:11.351
♪ At all ♪

00:01:11.351 --> 00:01:12.994
(audience applauds)

00:01:12.994 --> 00:01:15.537
- My goodness.
(audience clapping)

00:01:15.537 --> 00:01:16.620
That last 'At all',

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:17.453
Oh my gosh!
(audience clapping)

00:01:17.453 --> 00:01:20.370
That was Joni Mitchell's
song, 'Both Sides Now'.

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:21.203
- Woo!

00:01:21.203 --> 00:01:23.840
- I mean, it's such an
important song in general.

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:25.260
It's just such a cool song,

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:26.410
like her meaning.

00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:27.243
- Oh my God.

00:01:27.243 --> 00:01:28.076
- I'm behind it.

00:01:28.076 --> 00:01:30.170
But then to translate it to
the meaning of the movie,

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:32.184
I literally couldn't
listen, you saw me going

00:01:32.184 --> 00:01:33.390
(host imitating)
(laughing)

00:01:33.390 --> 00:01:34.223
- I loved it.

00:01:34.223 --> 00:01:35.056
- While we were playing the clip,

00:01:35.056 --> 00:01:36.414
cause I was like, I will lose it.

00:01:36.414 --> 00:01:37.420
(laughing)

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:38.540
It was that.

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:39.373
I mean, it had to be.

00:01:39.373 --> 00:01:40.620
You're nailing an American accent.

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:41.453
You're singing,

00:01:41.453 --> 00:01:42.620
you're signing,

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:44.140
you're... It's such an important message.

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:45.181
Important part of the film, like...

00:01:45.181 --> 00:01:46.601
(audience clapping)

00:01:46.601 --> 00:01:50.480
What was doing that song
like for you in that moment?

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:52.217
- I mean the lyrics speak for themselves.

00:01:52.217 --> 00:01:53.050
- Good gosh.

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:55.150
- Yeah. I actually watched
a Joni Mitchell documentary

00:01:55.150 --> 00:01:55.983
not that long ago.

00:01:55.983 --> 00:01:58.670
And she said that song is the
work of her childhood's end

00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:00.260
and Ruby is at the of childhood.

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:01.093
She...
(indistinct talking)

00:02:01.093 --> 00:02:02.000
You know, she said the
moment in life when...

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:02.833
- Was so poignant.

00:02:02.833 --> 00:02:03.666
- Figure out.
- Yeah!

00:02:03.666 --> 00:02:04.499
- Well, you know who she is

00:02:04.499 --> 00:02:05.570
outside of her childhood identity.

00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:07.780
We also shot that scene

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:09.430
in the last week of shooting, I think.

00:02:09.430 --> 00:02:11.380
And, I was getting so emotional

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:12.920
about the film being over.

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:14.070
I'd obviously trained for so long.

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:16.580
And so the movie had been
such a big part of my life and

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:18.630
I am so close with Marlee, Troy and Daniel

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:19.572
and Lonnie Owen.

00:02:19.572 --> 00:02:22.180
I was just getting so
emotional about it being over.

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:24.230
And I remember I looked up
and I signed I love you.

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:25.890
And then I just got really emotional

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:26.800
and...
(host awing)

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:28.580
I forgot how the melody went at one point.

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:31.210
And it's actually the take
that Sean used in the movie

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:32.080
because I guess...
- Yeah.

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:33.530
- That's emotion that is not fake.

00:02:33.530 --> 00:02:34.363
It's real.

00:02:34.363 --> 00:02:35.840
There was so much love making it.

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:37.170
- Yeah, I'm gonna cry.

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:38.027
- And it was real.

00:02:38.027 --> 00:02:39.660
It was so real

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:43.120
watching her go through
each different take

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:45.990
but she did it with ease and I...

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:49.180
Of course it was hard
but she made it look so.

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:50.013
Such at ease.

00:02:50.013 --> 00:02:51.760
And there's so many factors that

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:54.640
it turned out to be the most
beautiful scene together.

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:56.530
And I have to say that

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:58.975
Joni Mitchell actually tweeted about

00:02:58.975 --> 00:03:00.741
- What!
(host imitating)

00:03:00.741 --> 00:03:01.574
- What!

00:03:01.574 --> 00:03:03.600
- Yeah, she Instagramed and tweeted me.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:05.333
(audience clapping)
- Oh my gosh

00:03:05.333 --> 00:03:07.740
- I know. I fangled hard.

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:08.850
I was freaking out.

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:11.200
I...Its my friend said, "Oh,
Joni Mitchell airted you."

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:12.033
And I was like,

00:03:12.033 --> 00:03:12.866
sorry,
(laughing)

00:03:12.866 --> 00:03:14.650
like, it was surely just
a fan account account

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:16.100
or something, you know, like
(laughing)

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:17.650
and I checked and yeah,

00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:18.550
like she...
- Wow!

00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:19.680
- She said incredible performance

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:22.690
and she was congratulating
us all on the nominations.

00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:23.659
And she just...

00:03:23.659 --> 00:03:24.850
I mean... As I said,

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:26.010
I was nervous about the song.

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:28.352
So that was just like the cherry on top.

00:03:28.352 --> 00:03:29.500
- Oh my God.
- Yeah.

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:30.760
I couldn't believe it.

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:31.593
- Though,
(indistinct talking)

00:03:31.593 --> 00:03:33.310
to seeing that scene
feel different for you

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:34.462
than actually filming it because

00:03:34.462 --> 00:03:36.620
your character comes in

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:38.570
and kind of boost her
confidence in a moment

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:40.460
where she's feeling shaky.

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:41.560
And I imagine you're acting,

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:42.393
you're in the moment,

00:03:42.393 --> 00:03:43.226
you're doing it.

00:03:43.226 --> 00:03:44.490
Imagine there was a
whole different feeling

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:45.430
while filming it,

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:47.050
but afterwards watching it,

00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:48.545
did it hit you in a...

00:03:48.545 --> 00:03:50.071
Like it hit everyone else?

00:03:50.071 --> 00:03:50.930
- Absolutely.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:53.900
I just watched it for
first and because of COVID,

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:58.000
I was not able to watch in a
big screen and with people,

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:01.500
I just saw a card they
send me in my computer.

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:02.544
So I...

00:04:02.544 --> 00:04:05.310
It was like probably a
couple of months ago.

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:08.620
We were in a screening
doing all this promotion

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:12.830
when I watched it with people
all around in a theater

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:15.080
and I cried so bad.

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:15.930
I mean...

00:04:17.477 --> 00:04:21.130
I was so touched by
especially by that scene.

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:22.790
It's beautiful.

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:24.920
I really got into it.

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:26.240
I didn't remember what I did.

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:28.840
I was just watching Amelia performing

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:31.100
and the music so beautiful

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:33.420
that yeah... It totally got me.

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:34.935
- I did sit next to
him and all I heard was

00:04:34.935 --> 00:04:35.998
(snuffling)

00:04:35.998 --> 00:04:37.564
(laughing)

00:04:37.564 --> 00:04:38.397
- Oh my God!

00:04:38.397 --> 00:04:41.945
I have never been more grateful
for watching a movie alone.

00:04:41.945 --> 00:04:43.017
(laughing)

00:04:43.017 --> 00:04:44.680
Its Like I do remember my kid,

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:46.730
my five year boy came into the living room

00:04:46.730 --> 00:04:47.880
after I was finished watching.

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:50.002
And he was like, "What's wrong with you?"

00:04:50.002 --> 00:04:50.835
(laughing)

00:04:50.835 --> 00:04:52.660
And I was just like, "Oh! so beautiful."

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:53.493
I was like...

00:04:53.493 --> 00:04:55.750
I was like, it was Ghastly.

00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:56.950
It was a mess.
(laughing)

00:04:56.950 --> 00:04:57.783
It's...

00:04:57.783 --> 00:04:59.957
Literally, I'm gonna keep saying it

00:04:59.957 --> 00:05:02.436
(laughing)
but it's such a great film

00:05:02.436 --> 00:05:03.269
(laughing)
and...

00:05:03.269 --> 00:05:05.030
(audience clapping)
give it up.

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:07.120
I have been dying to
interview these people.

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:09.810
Thank you so much for
honoring me with your time.

00:05:09.810 --> 00:05:10.643
- Thank you.

00:05:10.643 --> 00:05:11.620
- Thank you so much.

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:12.930
(audience applauding)
Give it up one more time

00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:14.483
